{"comment":"The registry of air-apps on a new host. ${home} is a home directory of the test, ${dir} a directory of its own, and ${project} a project directory with a Git root. The step file {path, text} writes a file, and fileRemoved {path} deletes it; the watch of air-apps sees each within its debounce, and a runner waits for the next frame. The IDE link is the connection of air-ide: the IDE is the client, and air-ide the host."}
{"step":"file","path":"${home}/.air/apps/fixture.yaml","text":"format: 1\nid: fixture\nname: Fixture\nserver:\n  command: ${dir}/fixture-app\n  args: [serve]\nviews:\n  main: { resource: ui://fixture/main, place: toolWindow, toolWindow: { title: Fixture } }\n  log: { resource: ui://fixture/log, place: toolWindowTab, toolWindowTab: { of: main, title: Log } }\n  review: { resource: ui://fixture/review, place: editor, instances: many }\n  settings: { resource: ui://fixture/settings, place: window, window: { width: 880, height: 640 } }\nactions:\n  - id: refresh\n    text: Refresh Fixture\n    groups: [Vcs.MainMenu]\n    run: { tool: refresh }\n"}
{"link":"ide","from":"ide","message":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"channel":"ahp-root://","protocolVersions":["1.0.0"],"clientId":"corpus","_meta":{"x-air-ide":{"version":"1.0.0"}}}}}
{"link":"ide","from":"air-ide","message":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"1.0.0","serverSeq":0,"snapshots":[],"serverInfo":{"name":"air-ide"},"_meta":{"x-air-ide":{"version":"1.0.0"}}}}}
{"comment":"appsOpen opens the held apps channel of one project. The snapshot holds every app of the registry, each with its views and actions, the defaults of the schema filled in."}
{"link":"ide","from":"ide","message":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"x-air-ide/appsOpen","params":{"channel":"ahp-root://","project":{"path":"${project}","local":true},"roots":[{"uri":"file://${project}","name":"project"}]}}}
